  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $P(z):$ $\\sqrt{z}<1$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $N,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The truth set of $P(z)$ is $\u2205.$\n- The truth set of $P(z)$ is $N.$\n- $\u2203z\\in N,\\,P(z).$",
  "worked_solution": "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n\u2203x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne \u2205\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\u2205.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The truth set is empty.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne N.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${T}_{P}$ is empty, the statement $\u2203z\\in N,\\,P(z)$ is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
